cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QualFrame in your research, please cite this software using the metadata below. Citation is requested, not an additional condition of the MIT license."
type: software
title: "QualFrame: AI-assisted directed content analysis you can check"
authors:
  - family-names: "van Allen"
    given-names: "Zack"
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZvanAllen/qualframe"
url: "https://github.com/ZvanAllen/qualframe"
abstract: "Local, open-source software for directed (deductive) qualitative content analysis with language models. QualFrame applies a researcher's codebook to interview transcripts, places every proposed code beside its exact source passage for human review, compares coding runs, and keeps a reproducible record of models, prompts, settings, and decisions."
keywords:
  - qualitative analysis
  - directed content analysis
  - human-in-the-loop
  - research software
  - reproducibility
  - CFIR
  - large language models
